1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,878
<i>I mean, it's wild. Abi is actually Bea?</i>

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:06,923
<i>The puppet master who's been</i>
<i>manipulating Caloy</i>

3
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:08,133
<i>is actually Abi?</i>

4
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:11,219
<i>What we don't know right now</i>
<i>is what her motive is.</i>

5
00:00:11,803 --> 00:00:13,096
<i>Your relationship with Caloy?</i>

6
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:16,474
<i>- We don't have a relationship.</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>You don't?</i>

7
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,937
<i>What did I ever do to you?</i>

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,817
[ENRICO]<i> How did you end up</i>
<i>living together anyway?</i>

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,738
<i>Billy tried to run away with Oliver</i>
<i>many times.</i>

10
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:31,656
<i>They lived in all sorts of places.</i>

11
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:32,657
<i>On the street…</i>

12
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,284
<i>Under the bridge…</i>

13
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:37,412
<i>That's when I decided to adopt them.</i>

14
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:39,456
[MAN] <i>Boss Zandro sent me.</i>

15
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:40,749
<i>He wanted to remind you</i>

16
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:44,627
<i>that no one has ever outsmarted him,</i>
<i>especially when it comes to money.</i>

17
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:49,299
<i>I'm glad you're back.</i>
<i>We really took a hit while you were gone.</i>

18
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:52,260
[CAMILLE] <i>I knew it wasn't a mistake</i>
<i>to give you another chance.</i>

19
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:56,556
[BEA] <i>Thank you again.</i>

20
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:04,355
I can't believe Pebblng still took Bea in!

21
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,816
We should sue that delulu poser!

22
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,401
I agree.

23
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,988
I think we should drag her down
on social media.

24
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:14,741
[CHARM] I don't know who's crazier.

25
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:18,369
The poser or the company
that still took the poser in.

26
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:21,748
Better yet, I'll just get
both of their asses!

27
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:25,668
They're getting into my… blood vessels!

28
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,504
Calm down, guys.

29
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:29,464
This is exactly what they want.

30
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:31,591
To provoke us.

31
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:33,218
What if

32
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:38,139
we redirect this passion
into something more

33
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:39,182
useful?

34
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:43,144
Like our pilot project
for Happily Ever After.

35
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:47,482
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

36
00:01:47,565 --> 00:01:49,192
And our first couple,

37
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:51,945
Melissa and Theo.

38
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:54,823
A cute and happy couple, at first glance.

39
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:58,576
They were already engaged
when Melissa called through LoveLine.

40
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,788
I got to talk to her,
and she mentioned that

41
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:03,957
her dad does not approve of Theo.

42
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,375
[MARIO] <i>Why bring us here?</i>

43
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:09,796
<i>There's an Italian restaurant</i>
<i>near my favorite place anyway.</i>

44
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:12,966
<i>Dad, I told you they serve</i>
<i>the best gambas here, right?</i>

45
00:02:13,049 --> 00:02:14,134
<i>Come on, you'll love it!</i>

46
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:15,885
<i>Just go along with your daughter.</i>

47
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:17,220
<i>Let's give it a try.</i>

48
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:19,222
[MARIO] <i>Okay. Let's order then.</i>

49
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:21,266
[MARIO] <i>Uh, waiter!</i>

50
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:23,518
[MAN] <i>Good evening, everyone.</i>

51
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:25,228
<i>Whoa, okay.</i>

52
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:27,939
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:29,315
<i>Isn't this…?</i>

54
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:31,860
<i>Uh, Theo, sir.</i>
<i>I hope you still remember me.</i>

55
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:34,404
<i>So, you're a waiter here?</i>

56
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:36,781
<i>This is our best-selling gambas.</i>

57
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:39,200
<i>Cooked with lemon, butter, and garlic.</i>

58
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:41,494
<i>It's my special recipe, sir,</i>

59
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:44,831
<i>so I made sure it's cooked</i>
<i>to perfection just for you.</i>

60
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:47,125
<i>Ah, so you're a chef then?</i>

61
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:49,252
<i>I'm a cook, sir.</i>

62
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:55,675
<i>The reason Melissa brought you here</i>
<i>is because, um…</i>

63
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:56,926
[MELISSA]<i> Uh…</i>

64
00:02:57,927 --> 00:03:00,179
<i>Dad, Mom,</i>

65
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,098
<i>we want to ask for your blessing.</i>

66
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:07,979
<i>Uh, I've already saved up enough funds.</i>

67
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:09,981
<i>Just a little more and I'll be</i>
<i>a business partner</i>

68
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:11,399
<i>here at the restaurant and--</i>

69
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:13,401
<i>- Honey!</i>
<i>- Dad!</i>

70
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:15,403
[BILLY] Melissa's dad

71
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:19,365
believes that Theo
doesn't deserve his daughter.

72
00:03:19,449 --> 00:03:24,829
Melissa is a critically acclaimed
children's book author and illustrator,

73
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:29,459
while Theo is a cook at a restaurant.

74
00:03:30,501 --> 00:03:33,254
Melissa's dad thinks she deserves better.

75
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,298
But!

76
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:39,135
They're both fighters
when it comes to love.

77
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:41,512
In the end, love wins!

78
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:45,767
They will push through with the wedding
with or without the father's blessing.

79
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,561
They stood their ground.

80
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,146
Mm-hmm.

81
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:52,106
Now we have this.

82
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:56,444
Kindly check for your reference
to get to know the couple better.

83
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:58,154
Please get one and pass.

84
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,657
Please get one and pass.

85
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:03,243
I'll pass.

86
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,411
I'm jealous.

87
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,456
What?

88
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:14,045
I mean, I love her style! It's so magical!

89
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:17,799
Maybe we can use this as inspiration
for their wedding, right?

90
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:19,717
Charm, great idea!

91
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,427
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

92
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:23,137
A fairytale wedding.

93
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:25,056
[TONI] <i>If we want it to be magical,</i>

94
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:28,476
<i>I know a supplier of crystals</i>
<i>and gemstones!</i>

95
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:30,270
<i>Not only for the aesthetic appeal,</i>

96
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:32,772
<i>but also for good luck</i>
<i>and prosperity as well.</i>

97
00:04:32,855 --> 00:04:34,816
[VALERIE] <i>I have a friend</i>
<i>who is a costume designer.</i>

98
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:37,819
<i>She can take care of all</i>
<i>the costumes that we need.</i>

99
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:39,862
[CHARM] <i>We can also collaborate</i>

100
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:43,908
<i>with our visual design production partners</i>
<i>from our previous marketing events.</i>

101
00:04:43,992 --> 00:04:49,580
<i>And Ralph and I also know wedding souvenir</i>
<i>and wedding booth suppliers.</i>

102
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:54,127
[BILLY] <i>But most importantly, we need</i>
<i>to be able to immortalize this event.</i>

103
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:56,379
<i>This can't be just beautiful.</i>

104
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,589
<i>It has to be meaningful.</i>

105
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:03,428
<i>It should be a testament to how hard</i>
<i>our couple fought for each other.</i>

106
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:11,394
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:53,311
What's going on? Why are you
only putting that on now?

108
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:54,896
What time did you even start?

109
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:59,150
Huh? Ma'am, look, it's crooked!

110
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:01,611
All you have to do
is line them up straight.

111
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:04,072
Your job's simple, so do it.

112
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,615
There's even four of you doing the work!

113
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:06,532
Hello, sir?

114
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:09,660
Wow, you've never left your spot!
You've been there since forever!

115
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,704
Every time I check, you're always there.

116
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,081
Go over there and fix things!

117
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:15,583
Wait, why is this here?

118
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:17,335
The LED display is getting blocked.

119
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,337
Move it aside here!

120
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,839
Put it over here.
Move it a bit to the side.

121
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:24,592
What the--? Just when did you get started?

122
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:25,927
Why do I still have to do this?

123
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,429
Morrie, where's Syd Hermosa, huh?

124
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:31,099
He's the event stylist, yet he's not here.
He only sent his people.

125
00:06:31,182 --> 00:06:32,016
What's up with that?

126
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,018
He's still not here?
Let me give him a call.

127
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:35,728
- I'll call him.
- Please do.

128
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:37,438
We're about to start.
It's driving me nuts.

129
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:40,233
What about the seating arrangement?
Have you revised it already?

130
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:41,818
Yes, I already told them to get to it.

131
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:44,362
You told them? But that's your job!

132
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:45,738
Why did you have them do it?

133
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,573
It's not that hard!

134
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:50,993
Hold on, calm down
with your bossing around.

135
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:52,328
We're equals here.

136
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,621
Hm?

137
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,791
I'm just nervous.
I want everything to be perfect.

138
00:06:56,874 --> 00:06:59,085
Sure. Perfect.

139
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:03,756
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:06,342
[MAN] Okay, look at the camera.

141
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:11,097
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

142
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,348
[PHOTOGRAPHER] Another pose!

143
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,350
[WHISPERING] Marj, let's try
to give off a happy vibe.

144
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,102
- [WHISPERING] Yeah.
- Her eyes.

145
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,061
Okay.

146
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:19,439
Um, Melissa?

147
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:22,316
Can we try, like, a bigger smile?
A brighter smile!

148
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,360
Like it's the happiest day of your life.

149
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:25,570
Is that okay?

150
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:27,029
Can we try one more?

151
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:29,073
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]
- Okay, smile!

152
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:32,869
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]
- Okay, happier!

153
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:36,873
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,833
Um, Melissa?

155
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,501
Are you okay?

156
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:43,379
I want to thank you
for making my dream wedding come true.

157
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,340
But it won't be complete.

158
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,009
Not without my dad.

159
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:52,013
- Marj.
- Sir, let's head outside first.

160
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:55,099
- Okay.
- Sir, let's give them space.

161
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:00,396
- You know, I'm an only child.
- Mm-hmm.

162
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,898
And I'm a daddy's girl.
[CRYING SOFTLY]

163
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:04,775
And the only reason
I believe in fairytales

164
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:08,571
is because growing up,
my dad made everything possible.

165
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:09,489
Mm-hmm.

166
00:08:09,572 --> 00:08:11,782
For me, his princess.

167
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:15,786
[INHALES SHARPLY] You know,
he gave me everything I wanted.

168
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:20,374
Except for the most important thing to me.

169
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,337
His presence at my wedding.

170
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:31,511
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

171
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:39,393
[TONI] Chief!

172
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:41,395
- Yes?
- Are the shots good to go?

173
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:43,356
Yes, they're editing it now for SDE.

174
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,732
But, chief,

175
00:08:44,815 --> 00:08:48,194
it's as clear as day that the bride
doesn't seem to be happy.

176
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,655
Hmm…

177
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:54,200
Let's just do our best
to make our bride happy.

178
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:56,494
Mm-hmm. Okay. Mm-hmm.

179
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:59,747
Hey, did you know?
I got these flowers on a promo!

180
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,582
- They're beautiful!
- Excuse me!

181
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:05,711
Chief, we haven't gone over
our estimated expenses yet.

182
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:06,921
Oh, very good!

183
00:09:07,004 --> 00:09:08,047
- Someone's happy.
- Perfect!

184
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:09,298
- Thank you, Blaire!
- Thank you!

185
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:10,424
How are things over here?

186
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:14,762
Sir, I told you that angle
makes it unflattering for the bride, gosh!

187
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:18,057
I agree. Let's try to shoot it
at an angle from above.

188
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:19,308
- Can we do that?
- Yes, ma'am.

189
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:22,019
Okay. Chief, what do you think?
Think it'll work?

190
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:23,521
Yes, we can try that.

191
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:25,940
Actually, I want to retake
these last few shots too.

192
00:09:26,023 --> 00:09:27,191
I'll leave it to you, sir.

193
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:28,234
- All right, ma'am.
- Okay.

194
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:31,487
That way, the set will be
included in the shot.

195
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:32,572
Correct.

196
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,156
- That good, sir? Thank you!
- Yes, ma'am.

197
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,617
- [VALERIE] Please include…
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

198
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,869
It says, "Happily Ever After." [CHUCKLES]

199
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,913
I thought I finally had that.

200
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:42,790
More like,

201
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:46,168
happily never after!

202
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,336
You sure about that?

203
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:50,006
Each fairytale has its own plot twist.

204
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:52,133
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:55,094
Just make sure the live feed
to the projector is synced to the cues.

206
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:56,053
- Okay?
- Yep.

207
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:58,556
- Don't forget.
- Dude, how's it going?

208
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:01,726
Let me see. The program,
the lights, the music…

209
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,060
The feed is live.

210
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:05,187
We've already rehearsed the cues.
Everything's good.

211
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:06,439
- You sure?
- Yeah.

212
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,607
Okay, thank you.

213
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,985
- Chief, this is so beautiful!
- Mmm!

214
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:12,445
This is hand-painted?

215
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:13,946
The artist did amazing, huh?

216
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:17,074
Yeah! I wonder who the painter is?

217
00:10:18,534 --> 00:10:20,703
[TONI] It's so cute!

218
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:23,706
Oh, there he is!

219
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,207
[JORDAN CLEARS THROAT]

220
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:30,087
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:50,191
What are you doing here?

222
00:10:50,274 --> 00:10:51,609
Joining you here

223
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,654
in your world.

224
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:56,072
What?

225
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:01,911
[YANI] Love…

226
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,497
I'm sorry.

227
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:10,878
I realized too late that
when you love someone,

228
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,922
you must also love
the things they hold dear.

229
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:17,510
Instead of being jealous over it,

230
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,512
I should be supporting you.

231
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:23,057
Rooting for you.

232
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:26,727
I should be your number one supporter.

233
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,730
Not just your Prince Charming.

234
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:33,275
I should be your sidekick. In everything.

235
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,114
[SMOOCHES] Love, I'm sorry.

236
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:44,453
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:11:47,873 --> 00:11:48,958
[JORDAN LAUGHS]

238
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:57,716
So, are we ready,

239
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,218
Team LoveList?

240
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,304
For the love?

241
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:06,559
[IN UNISON] For the love, for the win!

242
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:08,602
[ALL CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

243
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:15,693
["WEDDING MARCH" PLAYING]

244
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,044
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:35,463
Love the gown!

246
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:38,424
Care of Pebblng, of course.

247
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:42,052
Bea, I really love
the last-minute revisions.

248
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:45,514
So minimalist. So modern.

249
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:47,975
It's giving Korean wedding vibes.

250
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:50,728
This was their dream wedding, after all,

251
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,771
so we made it happen for them.

252
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:56,442
All right, we have 10,000 viewers
and counting!

253
00:12:56,525 --> 00:12:58,611
A lot of people are reacting
on Pebblng's live broadcast!

254
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:00,112
- [CAMILLE] Perfect.
- There.

255
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,198
[MORRIE] "I love the theme!
It's very giving!"

256
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:04,200
- [PHONE CHIMES]
- "I want a Pebblng wedding."

257
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:05,910
"Congrats to LoveFeast!"

258
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:06,994
Yay! [APPLAUDING]

259
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:09,038
"Manifesting this with my match!"

260
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:09,997
Here's another one.

261
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,666
"Lord, please, 2026 Pebblng bride!"

262
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,044
I like that. I hope we get more of them.

263
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:17,379
- Oh, definitely.
- Hopefully, the views go up.

264
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:21,550
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:26,764
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

266
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:50,704
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:13:55,709 --> 00:13:57,545
[CHIMING]

268
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:14,520
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:19,400
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

270
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:23,487
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

271
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:37,042
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

272
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:43,340
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:58,814
Theo.

274
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:01,567
May your happily ever after

275
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,445
begin with my blessing.

276
00:15:05,446 --> 00:15:06,864
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

277
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:12,328
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

278
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:19,168
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

279
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:30,721
- [MOUTHS] Wow.
- [MOUTHS] Wow.

280
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:41,398
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:49,073
[CELEBRANT] Dear friends and family,

282
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:51,784
we are gathered here today

283
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:56,747
to celebrate the union
of Theo and Melissa.

284
00:15:57,414 --> 00:16:00,376
And to witness
the beginning of their journey

285
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:04,630
together in love and joy.

286
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:07,758
[MELISSA] <i>My Theo,</i>
<i>I promise to be your home, your heart,</i>

287
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:09,343
<i>and your endless adventure,</i>

288
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:11,470
<i>now and for all the days to come.</i>

289
00:16:11,553 --> 00:16:12,805
[THEO] <i>Melissa,</i>

290
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:14,473
<i>I vow to walk beside you</i>

291
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:16,767
<i>through every dream and every storm</i>

292
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,019
<i>as your love lights the path before us.</i>

293
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:21,271
[CELEBRANT] <i>By the power vested in me,</i>

294
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:25,067
<i>and in the presence</i>
<i>of your family and friends,</i>

295
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,069
<i>I now pronounce you</i>

296
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:29,947
<i>husband and wife.</i>

297
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,951
<i>Theo, you may kiss your bride.</i>

298
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:40,708
[CLAPPING, CHEERING]

299
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:59,560
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

300
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:00,978
[GREG] The good and the bad…

301
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:03,313
Why are they on their phones?
They're ruining the coverage.

302
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:04,690
[GREG] You were there for me.

303
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:06,442
Uh… Excuse me.

304
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,027
What are you watching?

305
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:10,320
The Happily Ever After event.

306
00:17:12,448 --> 00:17:13,574
Okay, thank you.

307
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:17,536
They're watching Happily Ever After.

308
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:20,080
What the hell is Happily Ever After?

309
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,041
LoveList's event.

310
00:17:26,336 --> 00:17:28,422
At the same time as ours?

311
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:31,008
I swear, Billy is doing this on purpose!

312
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:33,844
Their live stream has 500,000 views.

313
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:35,763
How many do we have?

314
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:37,139
Answer me!

315
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,099
Twelve thousand, Ms. Camille.

316
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:42,936
Only 12,000 views.

317
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,065
[CAMILLE] God!

318
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:50,736
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

319
00:17:50,819 --> 00:17:52,362
You may now kiss the bride.

320
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:03,373
[GUESTS CLAPPING]

321
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:13,092
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

322
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:26,814
<i>Which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

323
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:29,149
<i>What's your reason for going after me?</i>

324
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:31,110
<i>I knew I needed your help, Ms. Billy.</i>

325
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:32,319
<i>Snake!</i>

326
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:34,488
<i>Of the two of us,</i>
<i>who's the fraud and the liar?</i>

327
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:36,198
<i>You! Jealous bastard!</i>

328
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:37,783
[BILLY] <i>Here, we're a family.</i>

329
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:40,494
<i>And in this family,</i>
<i>no one gets left behind.</i>

330
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:43,038
[DOCTOR] <i>Mr. Toledo is</i>
<i>cleared for discharge.</i>

331
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:45,290
<i>He may now be transferred</i>
<i>into your custody.</i>

332
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:47,167
<i>We have so much to celebrate.</i>

333
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,670
- [BILLY, THEN EVERYONE] <i>Cheers!</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>Cheers to that!</i>

334
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:53,340
<i>Hearts Island will be</i>
<i>our next biggest project.</i>

335
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:54,758
<i>Can we really pull it off?</i>

336
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:56,176
<i>Let's make a bet.</i>

337
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,554
<i>I can't win against you.</i>

338
00:18:58,637 --> 00:18:59,972
<i>It's Jordan's birthday tomorrow.</i>

339
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:02,057
<i>Your and Billy's birthdays are</i>
<i>only a day apart, right?</i>

340
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,643
<i>- It's a double celebration!</i>
<i>- Yeah! Let's go!</i>

341
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:06,270
<i>Isn't it your birthday too?</i>

342
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,438
<i>It's tomorrow, Grandpa.</i>

343
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:10,691
<i>What's your wish,</i>
<i>my dear grandson?</i>

344
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,192
<i>Happiness for</i>

345
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:14,361
<i>the people</i>
<i>I care about the most.</i>

346
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:19,575
[BEA] <i>I don't think it would hurt</i>
<i>to give her a proper scare.</i>
